From faeab8af2c744dacc44e338418615af49a654fc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zahary Karadjov <zahary@agent-harbor.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:30:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] test(vm2): AVM_DIFFERENTIAL, a native-versus-wasm
 differential driver

Adds `avm_differential`: one translation unit, built by the same CMake code for
x86-64 and for wasm32-wasip1, printing one deterministic transcript so the two
targets can be compared line for line.

The transcript covers the AVM's simulation results over seven hand-assembled
programs -- revert codes, gas, fees, nullifiers, note hashes, data writes,
public logs, call frames and instruction counts -- and, in addition, the world
state directly: the genesis root and size of all four AVM trees, the full
sibling path of note-hash leaf 0, every genesis prefill indexed-leaf preimage
with its low-leaf linkage, an eight-step mutation sequence with all four roots
after every step, a checkpoint/mutate/revert cycle, and sampled sibling paths,
leaf values and low-leaf lookups.

Everything allowed to differ between the two targets is printed with a `diag `
prefix, so the comparison can enumerate it rather than filter by a pattern:
today that is the pointer width and, under wasm only, peak linear memory.

`differential/` is deliberately outside every directory the `vm2_sim` and `vm2`
module globs collect, and is excluded from the recursive glob explicitly, so a
translation unit carrying `main()` can never end up inside a library archive.

`PublicTxSimulationTester` gains a `merkle_db()` accessor beside the existing
`contract_db()`. The two databases carry independent create/commit/revert and
the simulator requires them to stay in lockstep, so exposing only one of them
was an asymmetry rather than a safety property.

Default OFF and additive: with `AVM_DIFFERENTIAL` unset, no target moves in any
configuration.
